<section class="page-hero section-wrap"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><h1>A little context.<br><em>A wider perspective.</em></h1><p class="page-lead">A personal and professional overview of the experiences, interests and ideas that shape my work.</p></section>
<section class="bio-layout section-wrap"><aside class="bio-aside"><span class="section-kicker">PROFILE / 2026</span><div class="bio-facts"><div><small>BASE</small><strong>Fort Portal, Uganda</strong></div><div><small>WORK</small><strong>Technology &amp; digital products</strong></div><div><small>INTERESTS</small><strong>AI, learning, music, research</strong></div></div><a class="text-link" href="mailto:kastineaugak@gmail.com">Contact me <span>↗</span></a></aside>
<div class="bio-main"><article class="bio-block"><span class="bio-index">01</span><div><h2>Background</h2><p>I'm Kastine Augak, a Ugandan technology builder based in Fort Portal. My interests have grown around software development, digital systems and the possibilities of technology to make information and services more accessible.</p><p>My educational journey includes St. Leo's College Kyegobe and ISBAT University. I value continuous learning, independent exploration and the practical experience that comes from building and testing ideas.</p></div></article>
<article class="bio-block"><span class="bio-index">02</span><div><h2>Professional direction</h2><p>My profile and current work are connected to SomaGPT, an education-focused AI initiative, and Apex Web Services, a digital services venture. I am interested in thoughtful product development, web engineering, AI-assisted learning and technology that can work in environments where connectivity and device resources are limited.</p><p>I prefer solutions that are understandable, dependable and genuinely useful over complexity for its own sake.</p></div></article>
<article class="bio-block" id="interests"><span class="bio-index">03</span><div><h2>Interests beyond technology</h2><p>Music is an important part of my life. I play instruments including tenor trombone and saxophone, and appreciate the listening, practice and teamwork involved in making music together.</p><p>I also care about community, communication and sharing knowledge. Those interests influence how I approach collaboration and the digital experiences I choose to create.</p></div></article>
<article class="bio-block"><span class="bio-index">04</span><div><h2>What comes next</h2><p>I want to keep building, researching and documenting ideas that can make a positive contribution — particularly across Uganda and the wider East African region. This site is a living record of that work, the lessons along the way and the interests that sit around it.</p></div></article></div></section>
